<title>UK: Sunken ship a danger to navigation off Bombay.</title>
<headline>Sunken ship a danger to navigation off Bombay.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 13,761-dwt cargo carrier Arcadia Pride, which sank seven nautical miles off Bombay on Thursday, is a danger to navigation, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The vessel, which was loaded with 12,000 tonnes of sulphur, was lying on its side at lat 18 52.29n, long 72 40.34e. All vessels were warned to navigate with extreme caution and give the area a very wide berth.</p>
</text>
